1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:03,100
Where the hell is Shiharu?

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:05,980
Let's talk in person. Alone.

3
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:10,400
Please help me find Shiharu Nanase.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,150
So, what's your next move?

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:14,020
The same as it's always been.

6
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:16,410
Find my sister.

7
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:22,830
[Keita]

8
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:32,350
[log.8]

9
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:35,420
Bones again?

10
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:36,950
Yes.

11
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,980
Well, we can't do much else here.

12
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:47,940
I'll escort Kayoko Senba to the hospital.

13
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:49,290
Alright.

14
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:00,450
Where'd you get the battle scars?

15
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:05,250
Plantae?

16
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:07,150
I don't know.

17
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:09,730
It may have been Xin Ming Ah.

18
00:01:09,730 --> 00:01:12,020
Xin Ming Ah?

19
00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:14,810
The conglomerate trying to buy out Nichie?

20
00:01:14,810 --> 00:01:16,770
Why'd they attack you?

21
00:01:16,770 --> 00:01:18,800
Beats me.

22
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:22,870
If you want my information,
you'd better start spilling.

23
00:01:22,870 --> 00:01:26,120
I really don't know.

24
00:01:27,270 --> 00:01:31,850
Then do you know where Haruka Nanase is?

25
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:34,560
He's gone and disappeared again.

26
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:38,460
I bet he's somehow tied to this case, too.

27
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:44,770
I expect something juicy in exchange.

28
00:01:44,770 --> 00:01:47,220
Fine, just tell me where he is!

29
00:01:49,790 --> 00:01:52,510
This case has taken enough victims already.

30
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:56,120
A bit late to the game, eh?

31
00:01:56,690 --> 00:01:59,300
It's about damn time you took this seriously.

32
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:12,850
Is the man named Ushio
involved in this case as well?

33
00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:21,150
Professor Ishimizaki's daughter
was seen on your intercom.

34
00:02:21,150 --> 00:02:24,300
What is your relationship to her?

35
00:02:26,690 --> 00:02:32,220
I first met her at Ishimizaki's funeral.

36
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:37,000
We've met several times since.

37
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:43,160
We would trade stories about him.

38
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:47,740
The same substance was used
to kill Professor Ishimizaki,

39
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:53,430
and to make an attempt
on Haruka Nanase's life.

40
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:56,800
It was most likely used here as well.

41
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:02,960
These cases are likely tied to one another.

42
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:10,010
Please, just leave me alone.

43
00:03:13,070 --> 00:03:16,260
You know of Shiharu Nanase, yes?

44
00:03:20,130 --> 00:03:22,730
Please, tell us where she is.

45
00:03:22,730 --> 00:03:24,680
I don't know.

46
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:29,080
I know nothing!

47
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:42,680
Why is there an officer here?

48
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:46,340
Tomoe Senba was killed.

49
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:53,450
Her bones and her son Keita's shoes

50
00:03:53,450 --> 00:03:56,550
were delivered to Kayoko Senba's room
earlier this morning.

51
00:03:57,990 --> 00:03:59,820
No...

52
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:03,640
She was probably killed long before today.

53
00:04:04,670 --> 00:04:07,450
- This is my fault.
- No.

54
00:04:07,450 --> 00:04:10,430
It's the work of that organization
Senba is involved with.

55
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:14,580
She's to blame
for associating with them as well.

56
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:16,690
Besides, the actual culprit is Ushio.

57
00:04:16,690 --> 00:04:19,240
- But...
- It's not your fault.

58
00:04:20,310 --> 00:04:24,620
Hirama filled me in.

59
00:04:25,210 --> 00:04:28,220
Honestly, I can't believe it.

60
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:33,200
Nichie created a human clone, right?

61
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:38,330
That's so ridiculous,
I'm still not entirely convinced.

62
00:04:38,330 --> 00:04:40,680
Could you tell me more about it?

63
00:04:41,910 --> 00:04:45,650
Tada wants to trade information with us.

64
00:04:45,650 --> 00:04:50,340
Tell him what we know,
and he'll share his intel.

65
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:52,880
Including anything about your sister.

66
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:56,830
Yeah. If we find a lead,
you'll be the first to know.

67
00:04:59,290 --> 00:05:03,010
You don't want more people dying, do you?

68
00:05:06,610 --> 00:05:07,920
No, I don't.

69
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:12,050
What do you wish to know?

70
00:05:12,050 --> 00:05:17,680
Your sister was created to be
Plantae's founder, right?

71
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:22,950
Right. She's still alive.
That's why the deaths haven't stopped.

72
00:05:22,950 --> 00:05:24,980
Exactly.

73
00:05:25,770 --> 00:05:31,300
We think your sister
ordered a strike on Tomoe.

74
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:34,820
That accusation again?

75
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:38,640
Your sister is the Holy Woman.

76
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:43,580
Yeah. It's clear she could give the order.

77
00:05:45,210 --> 00:05:50,200
That's the first conclusion I reached
hearing Hirama's account.

78
00:05:50,950 --> 00:05:55,850
If your sister's alive, she's the mastermind.

79
00:05:55,850 --> 00:05:59,520
You're saying Shiharu had both Tomoe
and Professor Ishimizaki killed?

80
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:02,000
If we don't hurry, Keita's next.

81
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,350
She would never.

82
00:06:04,350 --> 00:06:08,410
Your sister's the leader of Plantae!

83
00:06:08,410 --> 00:06:09,800
- Say what?
- Calm down.

84
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:12,180
Shiharu wouldn't murder a child!

85
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:15,750
We're trying to keep you safe!

86
00:06:34,750 --> 00:06:37,620
Please wait here.
The President will see you shortly.

87
00:06:38,770 --> 00:06:42,660
You seem quite busy these days, Maehara.

88
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:46,790
How are your frequent trips to Nichie City?

89
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,220
I am always busy.

90
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:54,750
And underlings are made to run errands.

91
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:57,620
I expect you would understand.

92
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:04,510
I can quit at any time,
and find employment elsewhere.

93
00:07:05,310 --> 00:07:08,790
I pity those who do not have such leisure.

94
00:07:08,790 --> 00:07:14,770
Like underlings who obey their superiors,
only to be tossed away on a whim.

95
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:21,930
I appreciate your patience.

96
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:27,770
What can I do for you today?

97
00:07:27,770 --> 00:07:32,620
I wish to ask about the bills
that he has been covering up.

98
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:40,810
Maehara is re-evaluating the fees
you specifically requested we look into.

99
00:07:40,810 --> 00:07:42,410
It seems there has been a misunderstanding.

100
00:07:42,410 --> 00:07:45,100
Is that so.

101
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:50,000
Then I am allowed to speak the truth
in his presence?

102
00:07:50,530 --> 00:07:52,290
The truth?

103
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:55,230
- What...
- Though I'd love to talk more,

104
00:07:55,230 --> 00:07:58,020
I'm unfortunately short on time today.

105
00:07:58,020 --> 00:08:00,660
I will reach out,
so let us speak some other time.

106
00:08:01,530 --> 00:08:03,200
Understood.

107
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:10,790
I can see myself out, thank you very much.

108
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:23,810
I will handle this case myself.

109
00:08:23,810 --> 00:08:29,510
Sir, what is your ultimate goal
with Nichie Pharmaceutical?

110
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:36,410
I would do anything for the company.

111
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:39,310
I want you to trust me.

112
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,590
What is going on behind the scenes?

113
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:47,710
I have no "ultimate goal" for this company.

114
00:08:49,350 --> 00:08:55,620
I have my hands full cleaning up the mess
the founder left me.

115
00:08:57,850 --> 00:09:02,690
That man will come to you with a deal.

116
00:09:02,690 --> 00:09:06,730
If you do not accept,
he will go public with his information.

117
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:08,900
- And...
- Maehara.

118
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:11,630
I said I would handle this case.

119
00:09:13,810 --> 00:09:15,840
I met with Haruka.

120
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:22,050
He said he had data pertaining to Roopkund.

121
00:09:24,300 --> 00:09:27,540
He asked me where Shiharu was.

122
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:32,620
Can't you tell me the truth?

123
00:09:39,150 --> 00:09:41,040
What is it you want to do?

124
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:48,180
I will obey your every order, sir.

125
00:09:49,910 --> 00:09:53,060
I will stick to my convictions.

126
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:55,960
You will stick to yours.

127
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:08,550
Even if our goals differ?

128
00:10:10,710 --> 00:10:12,290
That's right.

129
00:10:18,050 --> 00:10:25,890
[Is his step-sister the mastermind?]
[The truth shrouded in mystery and betrayal]

130
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:42,010
Excuse me, an individual claiming to be
Senba's relative has come to visit.

131
00:10:42,510 --> 00:10:43,870
Let them through.

132
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:52,220
Nanase!

133
00:10:57,350 --> 00:10:59,410
I'm sorry about earlier.

134
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:02,830
I should've been more considerate.

135
00:11:03,650 --> 00:11:07,250
But I want to solve this.
You have to understand.

136
00:11:09,150 --> 00:11:14,270
Can you tell me more
about this cloning tech?

137
00:11:14,270 --> 00:11:17,480
You have evidence to prove it exists, right?

138
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:19,750
Otherwise you wouldn't be so certain.

139
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:23,020
If you have something,
they'll come after you.

140
00:11:23,020 --> 00:11:25,100
I don't want anyone else to die.

141
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,520
Could you entrust it with us?

142
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:28,850
I already destroyed it.

143
00:11:28,850 --> 00:11:30,130
What?

144
00:11:30,130 --> 00:11:32,700
There never was any evidence.

145
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:35,250
Quit messing around, a child is in danger!

146
00:11:35,250 --> 00:11:37,950
You said I had no sister.

147
00:11:38,830 --> 00:11:41,960
Why would I have evidence
of a person who never existed?

148
00:11:42,530 --> 00:11:46,040
- You...
- I never lied to you people, not once!

149
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:51,850
Would this have happened
if you had actually listened?

150
00:11:51,850 --> 00:11:53,530
But no one believed me.

151
00:11:53,530 --> 00:11:54,980
That's not true.

152
00:11:54,980 --> 00:11:56,780
We looked into what you said.

153
00:11:56,780 --> 00:11:59,330
And that didn't stop the deaths, did it?

154
00:12:00,060 --> 00:12:04,480
If they weren't going to believe
in the first place, evidence won't help.

155
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:07,080
- That's not true.
- But it is.

156
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:08,700
Besides...

157
00:12:09,850 --> 00:12:12,240
You people can't stop this now.

158
00:12:24,270 --> 00:12:27,040
Dr. Senba, it's Kasuga. I'm coming in.

159
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:32,170
Goodness, you look terrible.

160
00:12:33,730 --> 00:12:36,160
I want to help you.

161
00:12:40,710 --> 00:12:44,990
If you're scared to return home,
come with us.

162
00:12:44,990 --> 00:12:48,460
We're all worried about you, Dr. Senba.

163
00:12:50,850 --> 00:12:54,230
So long as we remain in touch, you may leave.

164
00:12:54,230 --> 00:12:56,940
I will come to ask questions another day.

165
00:12:56,940 --> 00:12:59,670
- But...
- You do not need to worry.

166
00:12:59,670 --> 00:13:02,340
Just come with me.

167
00:13:04,430 --> 00:13:08,790
- Yes?
- That way, everyone will be safe.

168
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:32,220
What is going on here?

169
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:35,740
Will you people kill me next?

170
00:13:35,740 --> 00:13:38,520
You do not need to worry.

171
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:41,250
We are doing this to protect you.

172
00:13:49,810 --> 00:13:53,220
Please, tell me what happened.

173
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:59,050
I need you to tell me the truth.

174
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:05,150
I know you met Haruka Nanase
at Ishimizaki's grave.

175
00:14:05,150 --> 00:14:08,270
I had been tailing you both.

176
00:14:08,270 --> 00:14:11,120
What did you tell him? Out with it!

177
00:14:16,020 --> 00:14:21,310
I have a duty to protect my family.

178
00:14:21,310 --> 00:14:26,200
So please, tell me what happened.

179
00:14:31,310 --> 00:14:33,500
Keita...

180
00:14:36,020 --> 00:14:37,620
Where is Keita?

181
00:14:49,850 --> 00:14:53,040
Haruka? Did you figure something out?

182
00:14:53,690 --> 00:14:56,350
You shouldn't associate with me any more.

183
00:14:56,350 --> 00:14:58,200
<i>What? Why?</i>

184
00:14:59,060 --> 00:15:02,720
I met Mayuzumi yesterday.

185
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:07,520
We were actually supposed to
see each other today as well.

186
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:09,600
The investigator?

187
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:13,000
<i>She said she wants to search for Shiharu.</i>

188
00:15:13,540 --> 00:15:14,790
What?

189
00:15:15,530 --> 00:15:18,440
She told me Shiharu doesn't exist.

190
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:24,020
That's because she doesn't appear
on any family register.

191
00:15:24,020 --> 00:15:26,500
<i>But apparently that's a thing
that can happen.</i>

192
00:15:27,230 --> 00:15:29,100
So?

193
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:37,320
Mayuzumi says we can get her documented
as someone without a registry.

194
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:42,900
<i>I thought it wouldn't be a bad idea
to get her involved in the search.</i>

195
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:45,000
She'd be able to protect me, too.

196
00:15:47,810 --> 00:15:50,790
I think you're better off lying low for now.

197
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:54,160
Any one of us could be killed off next.

198
00:15:57,200 --> 00:16:01,410
I can't stand not being able to do anything.

199
00:16:02,150 --> 00:16:05,400
Everyone's only focused on
their own selfish goals.

200
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:10,290
No one actually cares about
whether you, or Shiharu are safe.

201
00:16:13,310 --> 00:16:15,310
<i>Are you outside right now?</i>

202
00:16:15,310 --> 00:16:16,910
Yeah.

203
00:16:16,910 --> 00:16:18,980
<i>You should get home immediately.</i>

204
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:21,500
<i>You never know who's watching.</i>

205
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:26,170
Okay.

206
00:16:45,730 --> 00:16:48,100
You really came alone.

207
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:52,250
Of course. I am on your side.

208
00:16:55,270 --> 00:16:59,390
How much do you know?

209
00:17:00,070 --> 00:17:03,790
I am aware you created a human clone.

210
00:17:04,650 --> 00:17:09,380
One from a corpse at that.

211
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:13,310
And if I said I know nothing of it?

212
00:17:13,310 --> 00:17:15,760
Then I will go public
with the information I know.

213
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:22,620
It'd make hiding the young lady
far more difficult.

214
00:17:26,190 --> 00:17:29,160
Or do you think you can keep her
hidden away forever?

215
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:32,330
In this tiny country known as Japan?

216
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:45,000
I propose you move to China
with your daughter,

217
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,160
and start a business using your cloning tech.

218
00:17:48,770 --> 00:17:51,790
I guarantee your living conditions
will exponentially improve over there.

219
00:17:53,650 --> 00:17:57,000
I didn't realize Xin Ming Ah
dabbled in such businesses.

220
00:17:58,560 --> 00:18:02,310
I haven't disclosed the specifics
to headquarters yet.

221
00:18:02,310 --> 00:18:05,130
I am currently acting on my own accord.

222
00:18:07,770 --> 00:18:10,500
What can one man do to help us?

223
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:13,450
Let me be your salesperson.

224
00:18:14,310 --> 00:18:18,620
The rich will buy your technology
without hesitation.

225
00:18:19,450 --> 00:18:24,410
The public won't ever have to know
of you and your daughter.

226
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:28,790
You're expecting me to trust such a gamble?

227
00:18:30,230 --> 00:18:34,850
You have no other choice.

228
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:37,450
Do you?

229
00:18:40,270 --> 00:18:45,370
I am half Chinese, half Japanese.

230
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:48,940
In China, I'm treated as Japanese.

231
00:18:48,940 --> 00:18:52,050
In Japan, I'm treated as Chinese.

232
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:57,200
I do not wish to be bound to one country.

233
00:18:58,020 --> 00:19:02,830
I only trust the nation known as Business.

234
00:19:06,350 --> 00:19:10,120
Please give it some thought.

235
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:13,790
I will not give you a deadline.

236
00:19:18,270 --> 00:19:24,050
But I also cannot say
when I will disclose the truth.

237
00:19:25,490 --> 00:19:30,800
Perhaps in a year. Or maybe tomorrow.

238
00:19:53,050 --> 00:19:54,490
Yes?

239
00:19:54,490 --> 00:19:57,620
Kayoko Senba is currently under our care.

240
00:19:57,620 --> 00:20:02,690
I plan to ask what happened to her.

241
00:20:02,690 --> 00:20:04,670
Is that fine by you?

242
00:20:04,670 --> 00:20:06,870
Why would I have issue with that?

243
00:20:06,870 --> 00:20:10,250
Your stepson is involved, for one.

244
00:20:11,230 --> 00:20:13,370
<i>I see.</i>

245
00:20:13,370 --> 00:20:16,560
When she speaks, tell me everything.

246
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:17,910
<i>Of course.</i>

247
00:20:27,790 --> 00:20:30,790
<i>Tomoe Senba was killed.</i>

248
00:20:30,790 --> 00:20:32,600
Hey, wait.

249
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:39,060
<i>Everyone's connected somehow.</i>

250
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:43,370
<i>If you have something,
they'll come after you.</i>

251
00:20:43,370 --> 00:20:46,840
<i>These people are killing folks left and right</i>

252
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:50,960
<i>all to keep this girl under wraps.</i>

253
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:05,550
Good evening.

254
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:08,620
- You're still here?
- Yeah.

255
00:21:08,620 --> 00:21:11,290
I'm organizing everything we know so far.

256
00:21:12,820 --> 00:21:16,480
This is a huge case we've got here.

257
00:21:17,110 --> 00:21:19,980
A clone? Is that true?

258
00:21:19,980 --> 00:21:25,740
I only half believe it myself.
I'll try pressing Plantae about it.

259
00:21:25,740 --> 00:21:28,430
Can't wait to see how they respond.

260
00:21:49,830 --> 00:21:51,400
<i>I'm home.</i>

261
00:21:54,490 --> 00:21:56,250
Welcome back.

262
00:21:56,250 --> 00:21:57,720
You're always sitting there, aren't you?

263
00:21:57,720 --> 00:22:00,740
Yeah. I wait for you to come home.

264
00:22:00,740 --> 00:22:02,120
That's why?

265
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:03,950
Yup.

266
00:22:03,950 --> 00:22:09,320
It's actually pretty nice,
waiting for someone.

267
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:11,500
You enjoy waiting?

268
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:12,890
I do.

269
00:22:14,610 --> 00:22:19,360
If a friend kept me waiting, I'd just leave.

270
00:22:19,360 --> 00:22:26,290
I've never kept someone waiting,
nor been the one waiting until now.

271
00:22:32,950 --> 00:22:34,660
It feels nice today.

272
00:22:34,660 --> 00:22:36,650
It does.

273
00:22:36,650 --> 00:22:40,170
- It's gotten warmer.
- Yeah.

274
00:22:43,570 --> 00:22:48,720
Don't forget I'm waiting, okay?

275
00:22:51,430 --> 00:22:52,880
I won't.

276
00:22:55,490 --> 00:22:58,000
You'll come find me, won't you?

277
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:07,940
<i>Shiharu is alive.</i>

278
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:11,850
<i>Shiharu is very much alive.</i>

279
00:23:21,460 --> 00:23:23,300
[Kyoichi Nanase]

280
00:23:23,300 --> 00:23:25,570
[Mikio Maehara]

281
00:23:33,150 --> 00:23:35,790
Want to know where your sister is?

282
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:38,250
Of course.

283
00:23:39,530 --> 00:23:41,260
<i>I'll send you the address.</i>

284
00:23:43,120 --> 00:23:45,420
How did you manage to find her?

285
00:23:47,950 --> 00:23:52,450
There's a building your father is renting
under the name of a fake company.

286
00:23:52,450 --> 00:23:56,750
You said you wouldn't entertain my delusions.

287
00:23:56,750 --> 00:23:59,450
What changed your mind?

288
00:23:59,450 --> 00:24:02,430
<i>I'm sure you plan to ambush me there.</i>

289
00:24:03,610 --> 00:24:05,850
I understand why you'd think that.

290
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:11,480
I'd make the same assumption if I were you.

291
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:14,700
Were you ordered to trap me there?

292
00:24:14,700 --> 00:24:16,510
No.

293
00:24:20,490 --> 00:24:23,660
I can't trust your father anymore.

294
00:24:25,030 --> 00:24:27,150
What happened?

295
00:24:27,150 --> 00:24:30,160
<i>I truly appreciate President Nanase.</i>

296
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:35,100
He took me in
when no one else believed in me.

297
00:24:36,950 --> 00:24:39,010
I don't want to betray his generosity.

298
00:24:40,690 --> 00:24:42,420
<i>Still...</i>

299
00:24:43,580 --> 00:24:46,870
I also can't allow myself to sit here,

300
00:24:46,870 --> 00:24:48,620
and wait to be tossed aside.

301
00:24:51,330 --> 00:24:53,010
Alright.

302
00:25:03,290 --> 00:25:06,300
- Kasuga, your approval please.
- Of course.

303
00:25:15,480 --> 00:25:17,010
Kasuga.

304
00:25:17,780 --> 00:25:20,360
The name's Tada, from the Kanzawa Station.

305
00:25:20,360 --> 00:25:22,330
I see no issues.

306
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:29,430
Kayoko Senba is here, yes?

307
00:25:30,250 --> 00:25:36,270
I believe Dr. Senba's location was to remain
a secret for her own safety?

308
00:25:36,270 --> 00:25:40,000
We must confirm something with her.

309
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:43,290
Is this a part of an official investigation?

310
00:25:43,290 --> 00:25:46,830
I only wish to ask a few questions.

311
00:25:46,830 --> 00:25:48,580
I will pass them along,

312
00:25:48,580 --> 00:25:50,560
and contact you with her answers.

313
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:52,970
But she is here, yes?

314
00:25:53,780 --> 00:25:58,130
I wish to speak with Kayoko Senba directly.

315
00:26:03,630 --> 00:26:05,800
Excuse me.

316
00:26:15,160 --> 00:26:17,220
Please, try to eat.

317
00:26:19,060 --> 00:26:22,940
I have business to attend to.
Please leave us.

318
00:26:22,940 --> 00:26:26,080
Then I'll ask you instead.

319
00:26:26,770 --> 00:26:29,830
Your founder, Sojiro Manabe,
requested Yumihiko Nanase,

320
00:26:29,830 --> 00:26:36,540
the previous Nichie head,
to create a successor.

321
00:26:39,010 --> 00:26:43,430
Is that not the clone created
from the remains of Roopkund?

322
00:26:43,430 --> 00:26:48,870
Or as Manabe called it, the Land of Souls?

323
00:26:49,980 --> 00:26:53,120
What are you talking about?

324
00:26:53,120 --> 00:26:57,700
Those involved in the clone research
were Kayoko Senba, Kyoichi Nanase,

325
00:26:57,700 --> 00:27:01,450
and the now deceased Akihiko Ishimizaki.

326
00:27:01,450 --> 00:27:04,620
The Holy Woman they created is still alive.

327
00:27:04,620 --> 00:27:06,950
She's here, isn't she?

328
00:27:08,450 --> 00:27:10,540
A clone?

329
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:13,570
Now that is utterly ridiculous.

330
00:27:13,570 --> 00:27:15,520
You ought to get some rest.

331
00:27:15,520 --> 00:27:17,690
Where's the Holy Woman of Plantae?

332
00:27:17,690 --> 00:27:19,850
Freeze.

333
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:23,160
What's up, Mayuzumi?

334
00:27:23,160 --> 00:27:26,350
Was she filed with an arrest warrant?

335
00:27:28,370 --> 00:27:30,480
You are under arrest

336
00:27:30,480 --> 00:27:33,800
for harboring a fugitive,
and sharing classified intel.

337
00:27:34,760 --> 00:27:38,450
Tada.

338
00:27:38,450 --> 00:27:40,840
What the...

339
00:27:40,840 --> 00:27:43,100
What's going on? Hey!

340
00:27:43,100 --> 00:27:46,120
Mayuzumi! Let me go!

341
00:27:48,610 --> 00:27:50,180
You...

342
00:27:50,180 --> 00:27:51,420
Come on.

343
00:27:51,420 --> 00:27:54,080
- Let me go!
- Walk!

344
00:27:54,080 --> 00:27:56,600
Mayuzumi, what's going on? Mayuzumi!

345
00:27:56,600 --> 00:27:58,850
- I said, walk!
- Hey!

346
00:27:58,850 --> 00:28:00,720
Let me go, damn it! Mayuzumi!

347
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,940
Keep moving!

348
00:28:02,940 --> 00:28:07,780
He said the Holy Woman
created from the Roopkund remains

349
00:28:07,780 --> 00:28:10,620
is still alive.

350
00:28:12,540 --> 00:28:15,420
It's possible she is.

351
00:28:26,630 --> 00:28:30,250
No! I was set up!

352
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:32,730
Sounds like quite the ruckus.

353
00:28:33,560 --> 00:28:36,390
It's probably my fault.

354
00:28:37,030 --> 00:28:39,490
I'll go see what's going on.

355
00:28:39,490 --> 00:28:41,800
Don't leave me alone!

356
00:28:44,240 --> 00:28:45,950
Please...

357
00:28:50,020 --> 00:28:51,810
Alright.

358
00:28:52,410 --> 00:28:54,340
Let's go together.

359
00:28:58,570 --> 00:29:02,390
Hey! Let me go, damn it!

360
00:29:07,410 --> 00:29:10,740
You bastards are falling for it!

361
00:29:10,740 --> 00:29:12,400
Are you listening?

362
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:14,430
- Let's return to your room.
- Hey!

363
00:29:18,480 --> 00:29:22,720
I was set up! It's all a trick!

364
00:29:48,690 --> 00:29:50,260
Hello?

365
00:30:00,160 --> 00:30:03,220
I appreciate the swift response.

366
00:30:07,370 --> 00:30:09,690
I grew tired of overthinking things.

367
00:30:09,690 --> 00:30:16,390
I would first like to see the potential
of your "human cloning" technology.

368
00:30:16,960 --> 00:30:19,480
I suppose you do.

369
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:22,010
May I meet the young lady?

370
00:30:25,310 --> 00:30:28,080
She is currently being harbored
at a certain facility.

371
00:30:28,700 --> 00:30:31,920
One I'd prefer to keep a secret from others.

372
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:34,540
I understand entirely.

373
00:30:37,740 --> 00:30:41,900
This is your key in.
I'll send the address later.

374
00:30:41,900 --> 00:30:44,020
I will meet you there.

375
00:30:44,790 --> 00:30:46,430
Excellent.

376
00:31:08,850 --> 00:31:10,680
Mayuzumi.

377
00:31:11,780 --> 00:31:13,990
I'm sorry I couldn't come the other day.

378
00:31:13,990 --> 00:31:16,990
- It's fine.
- Things became quite hectic for us.

379
00:31:16,990 --> 00:31:20,930
Does it have anything to do
with Haruka Nanase?

380
00:31:21,620 --> 00:31:24,640
We think so, but we're not certain yet.

381
00:31:26,730 --> 00:31:29,390
You know Kayoko Senba, right?

382
00:31:29,390 --> 00:31:30,600
Huh?

383
00:31:30,600 --> 00:31:33,950
You were seen on her intercom.

384
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:40,250
Oh, at the time, I...

385
00:31:41,100 --> 00:31:43,110
Relax.

386
00:31:43,110 --> 00:31:48,810
I'm not asking you as an officer.
I'm just trying to help find Shiharu.

387
00:31:49,320 --> 00:31:50,800
Right.

388
00:31:51,660 --> 00:31:55,740
Dr. Senba is currently with
an acquaintance of mine.

389
00:31:55,740 --> 00:31:58,230
Will you come with me to speak to her?

390
00:32:01,610 --> 00:32:04,690
You don't have to talk
about anything you don't want to.

391
00:32:04,690 --> 00:32:09,120
I just thought Dr. Senba may open up to you.

392
00:32:09,120 --> 00:32:13,770
Did something happen to Dr. Senba?

393
00:32:13,770 --> 00:32:14,690
Why ask?

394
00:32:14,690 --> 00:32:19,890
Well, I wondered why she was with
an acquaintance at all.

395
00:32:22,150 --> 00:32:24,980
I'll tell you more once we're there.

396
00:32:26,060 --> 00:32:30,330
Dr. Senba knew your father as well, right?

397
00:32:31,480 --> 00:32:33,400
Yes.

398
00:32:33,400 --> 00:32:36,430
Do you think she knows about Shiharu?

399
00:32:38,900 --> 00:32:40,680
Probably.

400
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:43,390
Then let's go see her.

401
00:32:48,060 --> 00:32:51,770
Where exactly are we going?

402
00:32:51,770 --> 00:32:55,650
A place where my acquaintances often gather.

403
00:32:55,650 --> 00:32:58,580
Dr. Senba feels at ease there as well.

404
00:33:00,490 --> 00:33:02,560
No need to be so nervous.

405
00:33:02,560 --> 00:33:05,890
What I want to talk about
is unrelated to police business.

406
00:33:05,890 --> 00:33:08,530
Is that allowed?

407
00:33:12,190 --> 00:33:13,790
Be right back.

408
00:33:18,230 --> 00:33:19,940
Hello?

409
00:33:19,940 --> 00:33:24,030
<i>I'm sorry. Kayoko Senba got away.</i>

410
00:33:24,030 --> 00:33:26,000
What happened?

411
00:33:27,910 --> 00:33:30,920
<i>Everyone's only focused on
their own selfish goals.</i>

412
00:33:32,790 --> 00:33:35,080
<i>No one actually cares about whether you,</i>

413
00:33:36,520 --> 00:33:39,160
<i>or Shiharu are safe.</i>

414
00:33:41,410 --> 00:33:45,900
We're searching the perimeters for her,
but I think she's long gone.

415
00:33:45,900 --> 00:33:47,770
<i>I see.</i>

416
00:33:47,770 --> 00:33:51,030
I was about to bring Mari Ishimizaki over...

417
00:33:51,030 --> 00:33:52,190
Bring her anyway.

418
00:33:52,190 --> 00:33:55,390
I have many things to ask her.

419
00:33:55,980 --> 00:33:57,630
Understood.

420
00:34:26,840 --> 00:34:30,590
<i>It's highly likely your sister
is being kept here.</i>

421
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:39,370
Everything is going as planned.

422
00:34:39,370 --> 00:34:41,610
I'll get my hands on it soon.

423
00:36:57,270 --> 00:36:59,150
Mr. Nanase?

424
00:37:08,800 --> 00:37:11,370
Ah, you must be one of the staff.

425
00:37:12,220 --> 00:37:15,250
I came at Mr. Nanase's request.

426
00:37:17,670 --> 00:37:22,510
Where is the individual who was in this bed?

427
00:40:24,020 --> 00:40:25,990
<i>Where are you?</i>

428
00:40:25,990 --> 00:40:29,400
Some lab Maehara told me about.
He said Shiharu would be here.

429
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:32,270
Maehara... So was she there?

430
00:40:32,270 --> 00:40:35,690
No. I found Xin Ming Ah's Kojima, dead.

431
00:40:35,690 --> 00:40:37,000
<i>Damn.</i>

432
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:39,440
Kyoichi Nanase arrived soon after.

433
00:40:39,440 --> 00:40:42,390
I think he came to see if Kojima was dead.

434
00:40:42,940 --> 00:40:45,300
<i>Then Kyoichi Nanase ordered the hit on him?</i>

435
00:40:45,880 --> 00:40:47,660
I'll ask him.

436
00:40:47,660 --> 00:40:49,800
<i>What?</i>

437
00:40:51,620 --> 00:40:54,050
I'll finish this myself.

438
00:40:55,540 --> 00:40:57,980
Tada was arrested.

439
00:40:59,490 --> 00:41:02,310
<i>Something's odd about his arrest.</i>

440
00:41:02,310 --> 00:41:05,580
<i>I can only imagine it's their doing.</i>

441
00:41:05,580 --> 00:41:09,130
We know too much.
Who knows what'll happen to us?

442
00:41:10,290 --> 00:41:12,740
<i>We don't stand a chance against them.</i>

443
00:41:13,410 --> 00:41:15,700
<i>Back off while you can.</i>

444
00:41:15,700 --> 00:41:17,160
I refuse.

445
00:41:17,160 --> 00:41:21,190
They've infiltrated the police.
My workplace isn't safe either.

446
00:41:21,190 --> 00:41:22,940
If you keep pressing,

447
00:41:22,940 --> 00:41:27,300
<i>they'll melt you,
or arrest you for some bogus crime.</i>

448
00:41:28,690 --> 00:41:30,540
I'm going to go see Kyoichi Nanase.

449
00:41:30,540 --> 00:41:33,370
See him, and then what?

450
00:41:33,370 --> 00:41:36,080
I need to know the truth.

451
00:41:36,080 --> 00:41:38,220
<i>Don't do it!</i>

452
00:41:41,150 --> 00:41:43,420
I'll end things here.

453
00:41:44,530 --> 00:41:47,040
If you eventually can't reach me,

454
00:41:47,040 --> 00:41:51,160
publish everything in an article,
on social media. Wherever.

455
00:41:51,160 --> 00:41:53,300
<i>Everything? But you'll...</i>

456
00:41:54,940 --> 00:41:56,850
I don't care what happens to me.

457
00:41:58,400 --> 00:42:00,210
I don't care if I die.

458
00:42:02,860 --> 00:42:04,750
I just...

459
00:42:06,620 --> 00:42:08,910
I want to see Shiharu, one last time.

460
00:42:24,170 --> 00:42:26,000
Mayuzumi.

461
00:42:27,330 --> 00:42:31,210
You were with Plantae all along.

462
00:42:31,980 --> 00:42:33,980
Come on.

463
00:42:33,980 --> 00:42:36,560
You're working for them, aren't you?

464
00:42:36,560 --> 00:42:40,120
You're no cop. You're just a lackey!

465
00:42:40,120 --> 00:42:42,170
Move it!

466
00:42:49,940 --> 00:42:52,650
Sorry, cancel all my plans today.

467
00:42:52,650 --> 00:42:54,070
Everything, sir?

468
00:42:54,070 --> 00:42:56,000
Yes, everything.

469
00:42:56,000 --> 00:42:58,010
Understood.

470
00:43:12,450 --> 00:43:14,320
You called?

471
00:43:14,320 --> 00:43:16,020
Yes.

472
00:43:16,020 --> 00:43:18,500
I wanted to talk in person. Alone.

473
00:43:18,500 --> 00:43:21,880
I'm glad you're ready.
Let's agree on where to meet.

474
00:43:21,880 --> 00:43:23,780
<i>Alright.</i>

475
00:43:23,780 --> 00:43:26,420
Will you come to Yamashiro Art Gallery?

476
00:43:29,960 --> 00:43:32,040
That's where Shiharu is.

477
00:43:36,360 --> 00:43:41,000
I'll join you once I finish one last errand.

478
00:43:41,580 --> 00:43:43,200
Wait for me there.

479
00:44:28,690 --> 00:44:31,580
<i>I can't trust a word that man says.</i>

480
00:44:32,380 --> 00:44:38,450
<i>But no one else knows where Shiharu is.</i>
